<section class="inner-sec">
  <div class="sec-eyebrow">How it works in the shop</div>
  <h2>Every call answered, every real job captured</h2>
  <p class="lede">One receptionist covers the phone, the texts, and the website — answering what's routine, getting the vehicle details up front, and leaving the actual work to you.</p>
  <div class="svc-grid">
    <div class="svc"><strong>Missed-call text-back</strong>A call you can't take from under a car becomes a text conversation instead of a voicemail you clear at closing.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Answers the usuals</strong>Hours, location, whether you work on that make, walk-in or appointment, how long a job ties up the car — answered instantly, any hour.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Gets the vehicle first</strong>Year, make, model, and what's actually wrong — captured before it reaches you, so the callback doesn't start from zero.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Books drop-offs</strong>Real jobs go onto your calendar as drop-offs or estimate appointments, not into a voicemail queue you work through after close.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Never quotes a price</strong>It captures what the job involves and tells the customer you'll confirm the price. No number goes out that you didn't set.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Human handoff</strong>Anything that needs your judgment — a diagnosis, an odd vehicle, a scope question — comes to you with a summary of the conversation.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="inner-sec" style="padding-top: 10px;">
  <div class="sec-eyebrow">Who it's built for</div>
  <h2>The shops that run on the phone</h2>
  <p class="lede">If your shop isn't listed — exhaust, wheels and tires, upholstery, mobile work — the fit is the same: if the phone rings while your hands are busy, it belongs here.</p>
  <div class="svc-grid">
    <div class="svc"><strong>General repair &amp; maintenance</strong>Diagnostics, brakes, timing jobs. The caller wants to know if you can look at it this week — answered without pulling you out of a bay.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Detailing &amp; ceramic coating</strong>Every job is a different vehicle in a different condition. The receptionist captures size and condition instead of guessing at a package.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Window tint &amp; PPF</strong>Vehicle, number of windows, film choice, the legality question everyone asks. Captured up front so the quote you give is the right one.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Auto glass</strong>A cracked windshield is an urgent call and a same-week job. It gets captured and flagged while you're still on the previous install.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Car audio &amp; accessories</strong>Head units, speakers, remote start, lighting. Fitment questions get routed to you instead of guessed at.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>One-man shops</strong>Solo operators feel this hardest. Every call answered is one that didn't interrupt the work, and every one missed is a booking that went elsewhere.</div>
  </div>
</section>

